# The data files are hashed by "scripts/check globe still.mjs" to decide whether
# the globe still is out of date. git hands files out with CRLF on a machine
# configured for Windows and LF everywhere else, so without this the same commit
# hashes differently depending on who cloned it. The check normalises line
# endings as well, so this is the second of two locks rather than the only one.
*.json text eol=lf
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf

# Binary, so git must not touch it at all.
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.xlsx binary
